<title>USA: HL&amp;P'S South Texas 2 nuclear unit at 5 pct.</title>
<headline>HL&amp;P'S South Texas 2 nuclear unit at 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Houston Lighting and Power's 1,250 megawatt South Texas 2 nuclear unit was operating at five percent of capacity Friday morning and increasing power, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Palacios, Texas, was shut Wednesday afternoon after its turbine tripped off line.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>HL&amp;P is a subsidiary of Houston Industries Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
